+# Build menu hitches
+
+## Problem
+
+The menu rebuilt its pages every time they were shown. `switch(props.Tab)` in `BuildMenu.luau`
+destroyed the old page and created the new one on every tab change: about 450 instances for
+Shapes (64 cards) and about 370 for Colors (121 swatches). `show(isMenuOpen, ...)` in
+`Main.client.luau` also destroyed the whole menu after it slid out, so reopening rebuilt the
+current page. That gave a 30–40 ms frame each time.
+
+## Changes
+
+- **Pages are kept** (`BuildMenu.luau`, `keptPage`). Each page is built the first time its tab is
+  shown. After that, switching tabs only sets `Visible` on two frames.
+- **The menu is kept** (`Main.client.luau`). It is built on the first open and never destroyed.
+  It still slides in and out on `isMenuOpen`. Once it has fully slid out, `BuildMenu` sets
+  `Visible = false` on it so it costs nothing to render while closed.
+- **Same look as before.** A page that is shown again scrolls back to the top, and the rainbow
+  swatch restarts at hue 0. A freshly built page did both of these. The first open still slides
+  in from below the screen.
+- **No hidden work.** The rainbow swatch's Heartbeat update skips its work while the Colors page
+  isn't visible (menu closed or another tab selected). Before, the page didn't exist then.
+
+The first time you open the menu, and the first visit to each tab, still costs about what it did
+before. That one-time cost is expected.
+
+## Checking it in Studio
+
+1. Play (F5). Open the MicroProfiler with Ctrl+F6 (Ctrl+Alt+F6 shows it detailed).
+2. Open the menu with M. Click Shapes, then Colors, once each. These first visits still spike;
+   they build the pages.
+3. Pause the profiler (Ctrl+P, or the Pause button) and switch tabs and open/close the menu several
+   times. Then look at the frames where you clicked. Switching to Shapes or Colors, and reopening
+   the menu while it was on either one, should now look like normal ~8 ms frames, not 30–40 ms.
+4. To count instances, run this in the command bar (client view) before and after switching tabs.
+   The count should stay the same after the first visit to each tab:
+   ```lua
+   print(#game.Players.LocalPlayer.PlayerGui.BuildMenuGui:GetDescendants())
+   ```
+   With the menu closed you should still see `BuildMenuGui.BuildMenu`, kept with `Visible = false`.
